{"step_index":1188,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T23:34:17Z","thinking":"**Verifying The Proof**\n\nI've successfully completed task-1184 and confirmed speech output through physical speakers. The next step involves rigorously proving the system's integrity via two crucial experiments. I'm starting to build a benchmark, the un-elided volatile blackbox readback benchmark, leveraging `ops/runtime/volatile_crdt_proof.zig` to begin the process.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// ops/runtime/volatile_crdt_proof.zig\n// Un-Elided Volatile Blackbox Readback Benchmark for Sovra CRDT Graph\n// Forces volatile memory writes on every iteration to prevent LLVM Dead Code Elimination (DCE).\n\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\nconst print = std.debug.print;\nconst crdt = @import(\"sovra_crdt_kernel.zig\");\n\n// Volatile write helper to prevent compiler DCE\nfn volatileWrite(ptr: *volatile u64, val: u64) void {\n    ptr.* = val;\n}\n\npub fn main() !void {\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n    print(\" UN-ELIDED VOLATILE BLACKBOX READBACK CRDT BENCHMARK (M4)\\n\", .{});\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\\n\", .{});\n\n    var graph = crdt.SovraCrdtGraph.init();\n\n    // 1. Warmup Iteration (10,000 insertions)\n    var w: u64 = 0;\n    while (w < 10000) : (w += 1) {\n        _ = graph.insert_node(w + 1, .Episode, @as(u8, @intCast(w % 255)), 0);\n    }\n    graph.node_count = 0; // Reset arena\n\n    // 2. Volatile Sink setup\n    var volatile_checksum: u64 = 0;\n    const volatile_ptr: *volatile u64 = &volatile_checksum;\n\n    // 3. High-resolution Monotonic Nanosecond Timer\n    const t0 = std.time.nanoTimestamp();\n\n    var i: u64 = 0;\n    while (i < 100000) : (i += 1) {\n        const ok = graph.insert_node(\n            i + 1,\n            if (i % 3 == 0) .Episode else .Semantic,\n            @as(u8, @intCast(i % 255)),\n            if (i > 0) i else 0,\n        );\n        if (ok) {\n            // Force a volatile store to memory on every loop iteration\n            volatileWrite(volatile_ptr, volatile_ptr.* +% graph.nodes[graph.node_count - 1].version_vector +% i);\n        }\n    }\n\n    const t1 = std.time.nanoTimestamp();\n    const total_ns = @as(u64, @intCast(t1 - t0));\n    const total_us = total_ns / 1000;\n    const ns_per_op = @as(f64, @floatFromInt(total_ns)) / 100000.0;\n\n    print(\"[RESULTS]\\n\", .{});\n    print(\"Total Nodes Inserted          : {}\\n\", .{graph.node_count});\n    print(\"Volatile Checksum (Consumed) : {} (Blackbox Readback Proof)\\n\", .{volatile_checksum});\n    print(\"Total Time Elapsed (ns)       : {} ns\\n\", .{total_ns});\n    print(\"Total Time Elapsed (us)       : {} us ({d:.3} ms)\\n\", .{ total_us, @as(f64, @floatFromInt(total_us)) / 1000.0 });\n    print(\"Real Hardware Latency / Op    : {d:.2} ns / insertion\\n\\n\", .{ns_per_op});\n\n    print(\"==========================================================\\n\", .{});\n}\n","Description":"Creating un-elided volatile blackbox readback benchmark in Zig","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/volatile_crdt_proof.zig","toolAction":"Writing volatile_crdt_proof.zig","toolSummary":"Writing volatile_crdt_proof.zig"}}]}
